      "writtenOn": "2026-02-22T17:57:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This debug_dma_dump_mappings() causes build failure with CONFIG_DMA_API_DEBUG\u003dy, since it is not available in the hypervisor. We should #ifndef it in this patch?\n\nAnd BTW even without CONFIG_DMA_API_DEBUG, when I\u0027m compiling my Debian kernel with this pvIOMMU series, it is causing another interesting build failure for me: multiple `WARN: multiple IDs found for ...` errors (like those mentioned in https://github.com/maluka-dmytro/pKVM-IA/commit/69aeb1bd1f2973b62e4766aa972eb3a2c3f9f538). I haven\u0027t fully investigated the root cause (and I still don\u0027t know why it doesn\u0027t happen, for instance, with the Android kernel which does have CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF\u003dy and CONFIG_WERROR\u003dy too) but I see it is related to the fact that debug_dma_dump_mappings() has `struct device *` in its signature. When I replaced it with `void *` just for test, it \"fixed\" the problem for me.\n\nIt took me a while to narrow down that this debug_dma_dump_mappings() is guilty.",
      "revId": "c5fcb114d6350e4b9a05794a1575ab506a92532b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
